The night of 16 to 17 September, the desk merged 412 reports into #4471 and closed it.
Subject matching put all of them under one ticket. #4471 is the `sched-prod` issue. Two other issues were merged into it by mistake.

## What the reports show

The export holds 427 rows. 15 are repeats of an earlier row, so 412 unique reports remain.
The desk's code files a report under its place and its error code (`fingerprint.ts`).
Grouping the 412 reports that way gives three desk issues:

| Issue | Reports | Reporters | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| `sched-prod` · E-TZ-114 | 349 | 205 | Shifts show one hour late. |
| `tram-3` · E-TZ-114 | 44 | 26 | Departure boards show trams one hour late. Same code as above, different product. |
| `rota-6` · E-SYNC-04 | 19 | 9 | Night shift listed twice. A different code and a different bug. |

## What was misfiled

#4471 is the `sched-prod` · E-TZ-114 issue. It already has its ticket.
The `tram-3` reports carry the same code, but the desk's rule treats the same code from another place as another bug.
The `rota-6` reports carry a different code.
These two issues have their own tickets, #2 and #3, and both stay open. Neither has a follow-up yet.
Both show a one-hour offset, so they may share a cause with #4471. The reports do not prove it.

## Why one ticket

The desk merges on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
Reports with the same subject went together, even when the product or code differed.
Reports with other subjects about the same issue would have been split. The rule does not read the body or the code.

## Not separate issues

Some reports also name `E-UI-31` or `E-NET-03`. The desk's code treats these as messages from the client app. No ticket was opened for them.

## Open questions

- Nine report IDs in the range R-41200 to R-41620 are not in the export: R-41207, R-41226, R-41307, R-41326, R-41407, R-41426, R-41507, R-41526, R-41607.
- Whether one cause explains the one-hour shift in `sched-prod`, `tram-3` and `rota-6`. The reports alone do not show it.
- Whether change #29 fixed `tram-3` and `rota-6`. Their reports stop before 06:15, so the data cannot show it.

## Lessons

- Merge on the place and the code. The subject line is not enough.
- A ticket that holds two issues needs a split before it closes.

